mponents (10)\nStability (10)\nDesign (10)\nDurability (9)\nValue (8)\n11/14/2024\nSo disappointed. Wobbly junk.\n\nOrdered the Besta TV stand and loved it! Very sturdy. However, we wanted something bigger. This is not the same sturdy quality. Very wobbly!!! Returning the first purchase was such an ordeal, I do not look forward to going through that again. I'd like to try brackets in each corner to see if it will help with the wobbling, but I'm undecided. I'll update if I do.\n\nAnonymous reviewer\nReport\nHelpful? (63)\n10/09/2024\nFell apart within a year\n\nThe doors never stayed aligned and the frame started sagging in the middle. The cam locks loosen over time and the whole unit shifts. Expected better for the price. Would not recommend for daily use.\n\nAnonymous reviewer\nReport\nHelpful? (12)\n09/17/2026\nLooks good, functions bad\n\nThe flimsy wood for the frame and plastic cam locks seriously degrade the quality of the overall product. The doors very easily misalign if the cabinet is nudged in any way. As soon as you go to open it, put something on top of it or take it off, the whole cabinet frame shifts, and the doors become misaligned. Not worth the price- this is weak sauce.\n\nDylan\nReport\nHelpful? (1)\nResponse from IKEA: · 09/20/2026\n\nOh no, we're sorry to hear this! You're welcome to visit our Returns Desk within 180 days of the purchase date with your receipt, and one of our co-workers will be happy to help you.\n\n01/11/2025\nDecent but tricky assembly\n\nThe end result looks good, but aligning the doors took patience. The push-open hinges are finicky and the instructions could be clearer for the hinge step.\n\nAnonymous reviewer\nReport\nHelpful? (3)\n05/21/2026\nGreat value for the price\n\nSolid storage for the money. One door needed adjusting but otherwise sturdy and clean looking. The push-open hinges work well once dialed in.\n\nJames\nReport\nHelpful? (5)\n08/02/2026\nBeautiful and spacious\n\nLooks stunning in our hallway and holds far more than expected. Assembly took about an hour and the instructions were clear. The oak effect finish looks much more expensive than it is. Very happy with this purchase.\n\nMaria\nReport\nHelpful? (8)"
